rc=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a73dc547d1c3a898.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a73dc547d1c3a898.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-9e7d867ab9581f20.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-9e7d867ab9581f20.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-9e7d867ab9581f20.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-9be6ab7e6f096913.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-9be6ab7e6f096913.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-9be6ab7e6f096913.png\">"],"answer":3,"solution":"The major product $($ s) obtained in the given reaction are<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-47c13a0f4baef53d.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-47c13a0f4baef53d.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-47c13a0f4baef53d.png\"><br/>The mechanism for the above given reaction is as follows. When the $\\pi$ -electrons of the alkene approach a molecule of $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$, one of the bromine atom accepts them and releases the shared electrons to the other<br/>bromine atom. A cyclic bromonium ion is formed.<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-0d9d3751ce05256e.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-0d9d3751ce05256e.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-0d9d3751ce05256e.png\"><br/>In next step $\\mathrm{Br}^{-}$ attacks a carbon atom of the bromonium ion. This release the strain in the three  membered ring and form a vicinal dibromide.<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-f6ce04cdf7e03be5.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f6ce04cdf7e03be5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f6ce04cdf7e03be5.png\">","difficulty":"Easy","source":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","_book":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430","_chapterKey":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430__68f8d4375694d9c689598ed9__68f8d4385694d9c689598edc__68f8d44b5694d9c689598eec","_marksId":"67c994efcc180496584ed4f0","question":"The major products obtained in the following reaction is/are<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-bf2a35ce3f4a6533.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-bf2a35ce3f4a6533.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-bf2a35ce3f4a6533.png\">"},{"id":310599,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","q":"The correct set(s) of reactions to synthesize benzoic acid starting from benzene is/are","options":["(i) \\(\\mathrm{Br}_2 / \\mathrm{Fe}\\)\r\n\r\n(ii) Mg / dry ether\r\n\r\n(iii) \\(\\mathrm{CO}_2\\)\r\n\r\n(iv) \\(\\mathrm{H}_3 \\mathrm{O}^{\\oplus}\\)","(i) \\(\\mathrm{Br}_2 / \\mathrm{Fe}\\)\r\n\r\n(ii) \\(\\mathrm{NH}_3, 25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\)\r\n\r\n(iii) \\(\\mathrm{NaNO}_2\\), dil. \\(\\mathrm{HCl}, 0^{\\circ}\\) to \\(5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\)\r\n\r\n(iv) \\(\\mathrm{CuCN} / \\mathrm{KCN}\\)\r\n\r\n(v) dil. \\(\\mathrm{HCl}, \\Delta\\)","(i) \\(\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{Cl}\\), Anhydrous \\(\\mathrm{AlCl}_3\\)\r\n\r\n(ii) \\(\\mathrm{KMnO}_4 \\mid \\mathrm{OH}^{\\ominus}, \\Delta\\)\r\n\r\n(iii) \\(\\mathrm{H}_3 \\mathrm{O}^{\\oplus}\\)","(i) \\(\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{COCl}\\), Anhydrous \\(\\mathrm{AlCl}_3\\)\r\n\r\n(ii) \\(\\mathrm{Br}_2, \\mathrm{NaOH}\\),\r\n\r\n(iii) \\(\\mathrm{H}_3 \\mathrm{O}^{\\oplus}\\)"],"answer":3,"solution":"Hi